    "Maintain the established presenter’s identity, clothing, and style for each channel; keep any additional figures purely illustrative and era‑appropriate.",
    "Preserve continuous narration‑image synchronization; do not use unrelated stock or decorative frames to cover visual gaps.",
    "Use the approved painted open‑world‑game aesthetic for all fictional scenes, ensuring props, clothing, and architecture match the historical period.",
    "Respect format‑specific pacing: apply short‑video rapid‑cut rhythm only to Shorts and allow longer demonstrations in long‑form videos.",
    "Include the mandatory CTA (like, share, save) exactly at the channel‑specified position; do not substitute with alternative calls.",
    "Base all visual and narrative choices on aggregated feedback and source‑supported facts; never create a rule from a single isolated error or topic.",
    "When correcting a visual mismatch, replace it with a historically accurate illustration, photo, or source‑backed graphic that directly references the spoken detail.",
    "Avoid overgeneralising a single defect into a style ban; phrase lessons conditionally and apply fixes only where the specific issue occurs.",
